Empty variable, empty text, no value, no type. Two unfinished stubs. They assert NOTHING: not a stat, not a number, not a bonus type. Only the COUNT is legible — two bonuses, which is how many the printed text gives.

fixes.detail:
THREE rows in scripts/data/effect-backfill.json, one per grade — the sigil, its greater and its major, because situationalBonuses.ts already carries all three and leaving two without the picker would just move the gap. Row for the base grade:
{"category":"items","id":"beastmasters-sigil","field":"effectChoices","value":[{"id":"affix","prompt":"What is the spellheart affixed to?","options":[{"value":"armor","label":"Armor","note":"You gain a +1 item bonus to saving throws against poison."},{"value":"melee-weapon","label":"Melee Weapon","note":"You gain a +1 item bonus to Athletics checks to Trip."},{"value":"ranged-weapon","label":"Ranged Weapon","note":"If you critically hit with the affixed weapon and the target is adjacent to a creature summoned with the sigil, the target takes 1d6 persistent bleed damage."}]}]}
Same row for "beastmasters-sigil-greater" with the bleed at 2d6 (item bonuses stay +1 per print). Same for "beastmasters-sigil-major" with the item bonuses at +2 and the bleed at 3d6 — which is what situationalBonuses.ts:1658 already pays. `id` MUST be "affix" to match every sibling spellheart, since the answer is stored under `<recordId>:<choiceId>`. Options are NOTE-ONLY — no `grant` key — because situationalBonuses.ts:1656-1658 already delivers the two bonuses; a grant here would double them. Verified the overlay can write this: applyBackfill() at scripts/lib/apply-backfill.mjs:56-66 does `target[fix.field] = fix.value` for any JSON value, and `effectChoices` is a recognised item field (src/data/index.ts:289 lists it among the mechanical fields that keep a record alive).
